---
// Live demo for Baustein transformerbloecke-und-attention: query meets key,
// attention you can check by hand. Learning goal 3 of the lesson plan: the
// roles query, key and value and the path comparison -> score -> softmax ->
// share -> weighted mix of the values, added to the old state. Pick the
// sentence and what the query of "Bank" looks for; every score is shown as
// a·c + b·d, the shares add up to 100 %, and the mix is added to the old
// state, which stays visible. All numbers are made up (two named places per
// vector) and labelled as such. Logic: src/scripts/demos/qkv.js.
import Demo from './Demo.astro';
import { SENTENCES } from '../../scripts/demos/qkv.js';

interface Props {
	lang: 'de' | 'en';
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const copy = {
	de: {
		title: 'Query trifft Key: Attention zum Nachrechnen',
		intro: 'Ausgedachte, kleine Zahlen, damit du jeden Schritt im Kopf nachrechnen kannst. Jeder Vektor hat hier nur zwei Stellen: eine für Sitzmöbel, eine für Geld. Die Query von „Bank“ trifft auf die Keys der Wörter davor.',
		note: 'Alle Zahlen sind ausgedacht. Echte Vektoren haben Tausende Stellen ohne Namen, und ein echtes Modell teilt die Scores vor Softmax noch durch eine Wurzel. Die beiden Query-Einstellungen stehen für zwei verschieden trainierte Query-Matrizen, etwa in zwei Heads. Anteile auf ganze Prozent gerundet, Mischung und Zustand auf eine Nachkommastelle.',
		sentence: 'Satz',
		sentences: { park: 'Park-Satz', money: 'Geld-Satz' },
		kind: 'Wonach die Query von „Bank“ sucht',
		kinds: { seat: 'sucht Sitzmöbel-Hinweise', money: 'sucht Geld-Hinweise' },
		vector: 'Jeder Vektor: (Sitzmöbel | Geld). Gestrichelte Wörter stehen nach „Bank“ und bleiben gesperrt.',
		step1: '1 · Die Query von „Bank“',
		step2: '2 · Query trifft Key: Score und Anteil',
		step2Hint: 'Score = Stelle für Stelle malnehmen und addieren. Softmax macht aus den Scores Anteile.',
		step3: '3 · Values mischen und zum alten Zustand addieren',
		solution: 'Im Park-Satz bekommt bei der Suche nach Geld-Hinweisen „Bank“ selbst den größten Anteil, 40 Prozent: Nur ihr Key (1 | 1) hat an der Geld-Stelle etwas, alle anderen Scores sind 0 und bekommen je 15 Prozent. Zusammen sind es wieder 100 Prozent, denn Softmax verteilt immer alles. Der neue Zustand (1,7 | 1,4) rückt kaum Richtung Geld, weil kein Wort im Satz Geld mitbringt. Im Geld-Satz bekommt „Geld“ dagegen 61 Prozent, und der Zustand landet bei (1,1 | 2,5). Welches Wort viel Licht bekommt, hängt also von der Query ab, davon, wonach der Head sucht. In echten Modellen ist es genauso, nur mit Tausenden Stellen ohne Namen und gelernten Matrizen.',
		goal: 'Probier es aus: Bleib im Park-Satz und stell die Query auf „sucht Geld-Hinweise“. Rate vorher: Welches Wort bekommt dann den größten Anteil, und ergeben die Anteile noch 100 %? Prüf danach dasselbe im Geld-Satz.',
	},
	en: {
		title: 'Query meets key: attention you can check by hand',
		intro: 'Small made-up numbers, so you can check every step in your head. Each vector here has only two places: one for a place to sit, one for money. The query of “bank” meets the keys of the words before it.',
		note: 'All numbers are made up. Real vectors have thousands of unnamed places, and a real model also divides the scores by a square root before softmax. The two query settings stand for two differently trained query matrices, for example in two heads. Shares rounded to whole percent, mix and state to one decimal.',
		sentence: 'Sentence',
		sentences: { park: 'Park sentence', money: 'Money sentence' },
		kind: 'What the query of “bank” looks for',
		kinds: { seat: 'looks for place-to-sit clues', money: 'looks for money clues' },
		vector: 'Every vector: (place to sit | money). Dashed words come after “bank” and stay locked.',
		step1: '1 · The query of “bank”',
		step2: '2 · Query meets key: score and share',
		step2Hint: 'Score = multiply place by place and add up. Softmax turns the scores into shares.',
		step3: '3 · Mix the values and add them to the old state',
		solution: 'In the park sentence, a query looking for money clues gives the largest share to “bank” itself, 40 percent: only its key (1 | 1) has anything in the money place, every other score is 0, and each of those words gets 15 percent. Together it is again 100 percent, because softmax always shares out everything. The new state (1.7 | 1.4) barely moves toward money, because no word in the sentence brings money along. In the money sentence, by contrast, “money” gets 61 percent, and the state ends up at (1.1 | 2.5). Which word gets a lot of light depends on the query, on what the head is looking for. Real models work the same way, only with thousands of unnamed places and learned matrices.',
		goal: 'Try it: stay with the park sentence and set the query to “looks for money clues.” Guess first: which word then gets the largest share, and do the shares still add up to 100%? Then check the same in the money sentence.',
	},
}[lang];
const uid = `qkv-${lang}`;
---

<Demo lang={lang} id={`qkv-${lang}`} title={copy.title} intro={copy.intro} note={copy.note} origin="simulation" solution={copy.solution}>
	<div class="qkv" data-qkv-demo data-lang={lang} data-testid="demo-qkv">
		<div class="qkv-controls">
			<div class="qkv-control">
				<span class="kev-demo-label" aria-hidden="true">{copy.sentence}</span>
				<fieldset class="kev-demo-seg" data-testid="demo-qkv-sentence">
					<legend>{copy.sentence}</legend>
					{(['park', 'money'] as const).map((key) => (
						<label><input type="radio" name={`${uid}-sentence`} value={key} checked={key === 'park'} data-sentence data-testid={`demo-qkv-sentence-${key}`} />{copy.sentences[key]}</label>
					))}
				</fieldset>
			</div>
			<div class="qkv-control">
				<span class="kev-demo-label" aria-hidden="true">{copy.kind}</span>
				<fieldset class="kev-demo-seg" data-testid="demo-qkv-kind">
					<legend>{copy.kind}</legend>
					{(['seat', 'money'] as const).map((key) => (
						<label><input type="radio" name={`${uid}-kind`} value={key} checked={key === 'seat'} data-kind data-testid={`demo-qkv-kind-${key}`} />{copy.kinds[key]}</label>
					))}
				</fieldset>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="qkv-stage">
			<p class="qkv-sentence" data-words data-testid="demo-qkv-words">
				{SENTENCES.park.words[lang].map((w) => <span class="qkv-word">{w}</span>)}
			</p>
			<p class="kev-demo-hint">{copy.vector}</p>
		</div>

		<div class="kev-demo-panel qkv-step" data-testid="demo-qkv-query">
			<h4>{copy.step1}</h4>
			<p class="qkv-big" data-query></p>
			<p class="qkv-calc" data-query-calc></p>
		</div>

		<div class="kev-demo-panel qkv-step" data-testid="demo-qkv-scores">
			<h4>{copy.step2}</h4>
			<p class="kev-demo-hint">{copy.step2Hint}</p>
			<ol class="qkv-rows" data-rows data-testid="demo-qkv-rows"></ol>
			<p class="qkv-sum" data-sum data-testid="demo-qkv-sum"></p>
		</div>

		<div class="kev-demo-panel qkv-step" data-testid="demo-qkv-mix">
			<h4>{copy.step3}</h4>
			<div class="qkv-mixcalc" data-mix-calc></div>
			<div class="qkv-bars" data-bars aria-hidden="true"></div>
			<p class="qkv-equation" data-equation data-testid="demo-qkv-state"></p>
		</div>

		<p class="kev-demo-live qkv-live" data-live aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-testid="demo-qkv-live"></p>
		<p class="qkv-goal" data-testid="demo-qkv-goal">{copy.goal}</p>
	</div>
</Demo>

<script>
	import { DIMS, OLD_STATE, QUERY_FACTORS, SENTENCES, attend, fmt, shareDecimal } from '../../scripts/demos/qkv.js';

	type Lang = 'de' | 'en';
	const TEXT = {
		de: {
			dims: ['Sitzmöbel', 'Geld'],
			turn: 'an der Reihe',
			locked: 'gesperrt',
			lockedSr: 'gesperrt, steht nach „Bank“',
			query: 'Query',
			key: 'Key',
			value: 'Value',
			score: 'Score',
			from: (state: string) => `Aus dem Zustand ${state} mit ausgedachten Faktoren, jede Stelle: Zahlen des Zustands mal Faktor, dann addiert:`,
			sum: (s: string) => `Alle Anteile zusammen: ${s}`,
			nothing: 'nichts',
			old: 'alter Zustand',
			mix: 'Mischung',
			next: 'neuer Zustand',
			sentences: { park: 'Park-Satz', money: 'Geld-Satz' },
			kinds: { seat: 'Query sucht Sitzmöbel', money: 'Query sucht Geld' },
			summary: (sentence: string, kind: string, top: string, pct: string, state: string) =>
				`${sentence}, ${kind}: „${top}“ bekommt den größten Anteil, ${pct}. Alle Anteile zusammen 100 %. Neuer Zustand von „Bank“: ${state}.`,
		},
		en: {
			dims: ['place to sit', 'money'],
			turn: 'its turn',
			locked: 'locked',
			lockedSr: 'locked, comes after “bank”',
			query: 'Query',
			key: 'Key',
			value: 'Value',
			score: 'Score',
			from: (state: string) => `From the state ${state} with made-up factors, each place: numbers of the state times factor, then added up:`,
			sum: (s: string) => `All shares together: ${s}`,
			nothing: 'nothing',
			old: 'old state',
			mix: 'mix',
			next: 'new state',
			sentences: { park: 'Park sentence', money: 'Money sentence' },
			kinds: { seat: 'query looks for a place to sit', money: 'query looks for money' },
			summary: (sentence: string, kind: string, top: string, pct: string, state: string) =>
				`${sentence}, ${kind}: “${top}” gets the largest share, ${pct}. All shares together 100%. New state of “bank”: ${state}.`,
		},
	};
	const SCALE = 3; // widest state in any setting is 2.5

	const el = (tag: string, cls: string, text?: string) => {
		const node = document.createElement(tag);
		node.className = cls;
		if (text !== undefined) node.textContent = text;
		return node;
	};

	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-qkv-demo]')) {
		const lang: Lang = root.dataset.lang === 'en' ? 'en' : 'de';
		const t = TEXT[lang];
		const n = (x: number, digits = 1) => fmt(x, lang, digits);
		const vec = (v: number[], digits = 1) => `(${v.map((x) => n(x, digits)).join(' | ')})`;
		const pct = (p: number) => (lang === 'de' ? `${p} %` : `${p}%`);
		let sentence: 'park' | 'money' = 'park';
		let kind: 'seat' | 'money' = 'seat';

		const render = () => {
			const s = SENTENCES[sentence];
			const words = s.words[lang];
			const r = attend(sentence, kind);

			// The sentence: visible words glow by share, later words are locked.
			const wordsEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-words]')!;
			wordsEl.replaceChildren(
				...words.map((w, i) => {
					const chip = el('span', 'qkv-word', w);
					chip.dataset.testid = `demo-qkv-word-${i}`;
					if (i > s.focus) {
						chip.dataset.locked = 'true';
						chip.title = t.locked;
						chip.append(el('span', 'visually-hidden', ` (${t.lockedSr})`));
					} else {
						chip.style.setProperty('--w', String(r.rows[i].weight));
						if (i === s.focus) {
							chip.dataset.focus = 'true';
							chip.append(el('span', 'visually-hidden', ` (${t.turn})`));
						}
					}
					return chip;
				}),
			);

			// Step 1: the query as a weighted sum of the old state.
			root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-query]')!.textContent = `${t.query} ${vec(r.query)}`;
			const calc = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-query-calc]')!;
			const factors = QUERY_FACTORS[kind];
			calc.replaceChildren(
				el('span', 'qkv-calc-lead', t.from(vec(OLD_STATE))),
				...DIMS.map((_, d) =>
					el(
						'span',
						'qkv-calc-line',
						`${t.dims[d]}: ${factors[d].map((f, j) => `${n(f)} · ${n(OLD_STATE[j])}`).join(' + ')} = ${n(r.query[d])}`,
					),
				),
			);

			// Step 2: one row per visible word, score worked out place by place.
			const rowsEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-rows]')!;
			rowsEl.replaceChildren(
				...r.rows.map((row, i) => {
					const li = el('li', 'qkv-row');
					li.dataset.testid = `demo-qkv-row-${i}`;
					if (i === s.focus) li.dataset.focus = 'true';
					const head = el('p', 'qkv-row-head');
					head.append(el('strong', 'qkv-row-word', words[i]), el('span', 'qkv-row-kv', `${t.key} ${vec(row.key)} · ${t.value} ${vec(row.value)}`));
					const score = el('p', 'qkv-row-score', `${t.score} ${r.query.map((x, d) => `${n(x)} · ${n(row.key[d])}`).join(' + ')} = ${n(row.score)}`);
					const bar = el('div', 'qkv-share');
					const track = el('span', 'qkv-share-track');
					const fill = el('span', 'qkv-share-fill');
					fill.style.width = `${row.weight * 100}%`;
					track.append(fill);
					track.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
					bar.append(track, el('span', 'qkv-share-pct', pct(row.pct)));
					li.append(head, score, bar);
					return li;
				}),
			);
			root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sum]')!.textContent = t.sum(
				`${r.rows.map((row) => row.pct).join(' + ')} = ${pct(r.rows.reduce((a, row) => a + row.pct, 0))}`,
			);

			// Step 3: share times value, added up per place; then old + mix.
			const mixEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-mix-calc]')!;
			mixEl.replaceChildren(
				...DIMS.map((_, d) => {
					const terms = r.rows.filter((row) => row.value[d] !== 0).map((row) => `${shareDecimal(row.pct, lang)} · ${n(row.value[d])}`);
					return el('p', 'qkv-calc-line', `${t.mix} ${t.dims[d]}: ${terms.length ? terms.join(' + ') : t.nothing} ≈ ${n(r.mix[d])}`);
				}),
			);
			const barsEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-bars]')!;
			barsEl.replaceChildren(
				...DIMS.map((_, d) => {
					const line = el('div', 'qkv-bar');
					const track = el('span', 'qkv-bar-track');
					const old = el('span', 'qkv-bar-old');
					const add = el('span', 'qkv-bar-add');
					old.style.width = `${(OLD_STATE[d] / SCALE) * 100}%`;
					add.style.width = `${(r.mix[d] / SCALE) * 100}%`;
					track.append(old, add);
					line.append(el('span', 'qkv-bar-label', t.dims[d]), track, el('span', 'qkv-bar-num', `${n(OLD_STATE[d])} + ${n(r.mix[d])} = ${n(r.next[d])}`));
					return line;
				}),
			);
			const eq = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-equation]')!;
			eq.replaceChildren(
				el('span', 'qkv-eq-old', `${t.old} ${vec(OLD_STATE)}`),
				el('span', 'qkv-eq-op', '+'),
				el('span', 'qkv-eq-mix', `${t.mix} ${vec(r.mix)}`),
				el('span', 'qkv-eq-op', '='),
				el('span', 'qkv-eq-next', `${t.next} ${vec(r.next)}`),
			);

			const top = r.rows.reduce((best, row, i) => (row.weight > r.rows[best].weight ? i : best), 0);
			root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-live]')!.textContent = t.summary(t.sentences[sentence], t.kinds[kind], words[top], pct(r.rows[top].pct), vec(r.next));
		};

		root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-sentence]').forEach((radio) =>
			radio.addEventListener('change', () => {
				sentence = radio.value === 'money' ? 'money' : 'park';
				render();
			}),
		);
		root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-kind]').forEach((radio) =>
			radio.addEventListener('change', () => {
				kind = radio.value === 'money' ? 'money' : 'seat';
				render();
			}),
		);
		render();
	}
</script>

<style is:global>
	.qkv {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--sp-md);
	}
	.qkv-controls {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--sp-sm) var(--sp-md);
	}
	.qkv-control {
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.qkv-stage {
		display: grid;
		gap: 6px;
	}
	.qkv-sentence {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 8px 6px;
	}
	.qkv-word {
		--w: 0;
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 5px 9px;
		border: 1.5px solid var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.2;
		/* Brightness = share: the more light, the more amber. */
		background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--amber-viv) calc(var(--w) * 60%), var(--ground-page));
		transition: background-color 0.25s ease;
	}
	.qkv-word[data-focus='true'] {
		border-color: var(--petrol-deep);
		outline: 2px solid var(--petrol-deep);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
	.qkv-word[data-locked='true'] {
		background: transparent;
		border-style: dashed;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
		opacity: 0.6;
	}
	.qkv-step {
		display: grid;
		gap: 6px;
	}
	.qkv-big {
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.qkv-calc,
	.qkv-mixcalc {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2px;
		font-size: 0.92rem;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.qkv-calc-lead {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	.qkv-calc-line {
		font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		font-size: 0.86rem;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.qkv-rows {
		display: grid;
		gap: 8px;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.qkv-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 2px 12px;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 8px 10px;
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
		background: var(--ground-page);
	}
	.qkv-row[data-focus='true'] {
		border-color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.qkv-row-head {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0;
	}
	.qkv-row-word {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.02rem;
	}
	.qkv-row-kv,
	.qkv-row-score {
		font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.qkv-row-score {
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.qkv-share {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: 8px;
		align-items: center;
	}
	.qkv-share-track {
		display: block;
		height: 12px;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--line);
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.qkv-share-fill {
		display: block;
		height: 100%;
		background: var(--amber-viv);
		transition: width 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
	}
	.qkv-share-pct {
		min-width: 3.6ch;
		text-align: right;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--amber-deep);
	}
	.qkv-sum {
		font-weight: 600;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.qkv-bars {
		display: grid;
		gap: 8px;
	}
	.qkv-bar {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 7.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: 10px;
		align-items: center;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
	.qkv-bar-track {
		display: flex;
		height: 16px;
		border-radius: 8px;
		background: var(--line);
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.qkv-bar-old {
		background: var(--petrol-viv);
	}
	.qkv-bar-add {
		background: var(--amber-viv);
		transition: width 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
	}
	.qkv-bar-num {
		font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.qkv-equation {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 6px 8px;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.qkv-eq-old,
	.qkv-eq-mix,
	.qkv-eq-next {
		padding: 3px 9px;
		border-radius: var(--r-pill);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.qkv-eq-old {
		border: 1.5px solid var(--petrol-viv);
		color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.qkv-eq-mix {
		border: 1.5px solid var(--amber-viv);
		color: var(--amber-deep);
	}
	.qkv-eq-next {
		background: var(--demo-c1);
		color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.qkv-eq-op {
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}
	.qkv-live {
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
		line-height: 1.4;
		padding: 6px 12px;
	}
	.qkv-goal {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.qkv-row {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
		.qkv-bar {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		}
		.qkv-bar-track {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
			grid-row: 2;
